"""Guides added 6 Nov 2026.
Opening a deceased family member's safe in Singapore. Legal facts checked 6 Nov 2026 against:
- Singapore Courts, Probate and administration (judiciary.gov.sg/family/probate-and-administration):
  probate = valid will, executor applies; letters of administration = no valid will, a beneficiary
  applies; a grant may not be required for estates not exceeding $50,000 if the Public Trustee agrees.
- Ministry of Law, Public Trustee's Office: may administer estates not exceeding $50,000, at its discretion.
- MoneySense, What is probate?: probate may take 3-6 months; grant taken to banks/HDB to access assets;
  Muslim estates: Inheritance Certificate from the Syariah Court via MUIS.
- Ministry of Law press release: Wills Registry managed by the Singapore Academy of Law from 4 May 2020;
  information released to next-of-kin or beneficiaries on application.
Owner-confirmed: checks NRIC, Singpass or other ID proof before any job; opens all safe types; issues
invoices. The exact documents Uncle Thomas asks for in estate cases are NOT yet confirmed, so the guide
says we'll tell you what we need and never promises to open on a particular document alone.
Not legal advice; points readers to a lawyer."""

